Careful: count for STRIPOFFSETS with data equals len(values) = number of strips (typ LONG/SHORT, not BYTE). Unpack count values. But if count*size < len(data)? write_long packs count*4 exactly. OK.

Also bigtiff? tobytes uses _pack("L") and entry format "HHL4s" — this is classic TIFF only (bigtiff writing not supported here). Fine.

